# Tasks: Song Leaflet Generation

**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-song-leaflet-generation/`
**Prerequisites**: plan.md, spec.md, research.md, data-model.md, contracts/, quickstart.md

**Tests**: Included and REQUIRED — Constitution Principle III (Test-First Development,
NON-NEGOTIABLE) mandates a failing test before any production code for new behavior.

**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story (from spec.md, priority order P1→P4) to enable
independent implementation and testing of each story.

## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`

- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies on an incomplete task)
- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (US1, US2, US3, US4)
- File paths are exact and relative to the repository root

## Path Conventions

Single project (existing `sb/sb.csproj`) — see `plan.md` Project Structure. All source paths are
under `sb/`; all test paths are under `sb/Tests/` (NUnit tests live inside the same project, per
the existing convention).

## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)

**Purpose**: Project scaffolding and dependency setup — no story-specific logic yet.

- [X] T001 [P] Create the new feature folders per `plan.md` Project Structure:
  `sb/Config/`, `sb/Index/`, `sb/Documents/`, `sb/Chapters/`, `sb/Formatting/`, `sb/Ordering/`,
  `sb/Leaflets/`, `sb/Cli/`, `sb/Tests/Cli/` (leave each empty except for a `.gitkeep` if needed
  — files are added by later tasks).
- [X] T002 Update `sb/sb.csproj`: change `<TargetFramework>net7.0</TargetFramework>` to
  `<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>` (research.md §1), and add `<PackageReference>`
  entries for `YamlDotNet` (research.md §10) and `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite` (research.md §13).
  *(Also added `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk` + `NUnit3TestAdapter` so `dotnet test` works, with
  `GenerateProgramFile=false` to stop the test SDK from shadowing `Program.Main`; pinned
  `SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3` to 3.0.3 to clear a high-severity advisory on the version
  `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite` pulls transitively.)*

