## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Generate a formatted leaflet from a list of songs (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Turn an in-memory list of songs into a complete, compilable single- or multi-column
LaTeX leaflet, trusting the user's own line breaks — one input line per output line wherever
space allows (phrase-splitting was in scope originally but removed 2026-09-26; see Phase 12).

**Independent Test**: Call `LeafletBuilder.Build` directly with a small set of plain-text songs
(no CLI/storage involved), choose single- vs. multi-column, and verify the output is a valid,
structurally-correct LaTeX document (per `contracts/leaflet-builder-api.md` and
`contracts/latex-output-contract.md`).

### Tests for User Story 1 ⚠️

> Write these tests FIRST; confirm they FAIL before implementing.

- [X] ~~T010~~ [P] [US1] Write failing tests for `PhraseSplitter` in `sb/Tests/PhraseSplitterTests.cs`:
  splitting on line breaks → sentence punctuation → commas (research.md §3), the no-punctuation
  fallback ("treat the whole line as one phrase" — spec.md Edge Cases), and cases drawn from the
  real fixtures in `sb/Tests/TestFiles/*.txt`.
  *(Superseded 2026-09-26 — see Phase 12: phrase-splitting removed; `PhraseSplitter.cs` and this
  test file are deleted.)*
- [X] T011 [P] [US1] Write failing tests for `LatexEscaper` in `sb/Tests/LatexEscaperTests.cs`
  covering every reserved character `\ { } % & # _ ~ ^` (research.md §6, FR-010).
- [X] T012 [P] [US1] Write failing tests for `ColumnBalancer` in
  `sb/Tests/ColumnBalancerTests.cs`: the `.475\textwidth`/`.45\textwidth` split with a
  `0.075\textwidth` gutter, and a `\vspace` appended to the shortest column(s) so columns end
  "within one text line's height of each other" (SC-003, research.md §5).
  *(SC-003 citation superseded 2026-09-28 — SC-003 removed; see research.md §5's superseded note
  and spec.md's new FR-007/SC-012.)*
- [X] T013 [P] [US1] Write failing tests for `SongOrderer` (AsListed mode only for now) in
  `sb/Tests/SongOrdererTests.cs`: given a list, `AsListed` MUST preserve "exactly the order they
  were provided" (Acceptance Scenario 1).
- [X] T014 [P] [US1] Write failing end-to-end tests for `LeafletBuilder.Build` in
  `sb/Tests/LeafletBuilderTests.cs` using real fixtures from `sb/Tests/TestFiles/`, covering:
  single-column output (Acceptance Scenario 1), multi-column output with balanced columns
  (Scenario 2), a phrase too wide for its column being broken across lines rather than
  overflowing (Scenario 3), rejection of an empty song list with a descriptive error (FR-012),
  rejection when `sb/template-main.tex` is missing/malformed (data-model.md `DocumentTemplate`
  validation rule), determinism (two identical calls produce byte-for-byte identical `Document`
