## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Order songs automatically or as specified (Priority: P3)

**Goal**: `sb documents build` produces a leaflet with songs either in the user's listed order or
automatically arranged for minimal unused space, bounded by `--max-permutations`.

**Independent Test**: Build the same document twice — once `--ordering as-listed`, once
`--ordering space-efficient` — and verify the resulting order differs accordingly and is
deterministic for a given input and choice.

### Tests for User Story 3 ⚠️

- [X] T042 [P] [US3] Extend `sb/Tests/SongOrdererTests.cs` with `SpaceEfficient` cases: exact
  search minimizing unused space when the song count keeps permutations within
  `MaxPermutations` (default 100, research.md §4), the deterministic greedy fallback beyond that
  bound, and deterministic tie-breaking (spec.md Edge Cases: "two songs are otherwise identical
  in space usage").
- [X] T043 [P] [US3] Extend `sb/Tests/LeafletBuilderTests.cs` with a case comparing
  `SpaceEfficient` vs. `AsListed` output for the same songs, asserting the former minimizes
  unused space/pages relative to the original order (Acceptance Scenario 2).
- [X] T044 [P] [US3] Extend `sb/Tests/Cli/DocumentCommandsTests.cs` with `sb documents build
  --ordering`/`--max-permutations` cases per `contracts/cli-commands.md`, including the
  not-a-positive-integer error for `--max-permutations`.

### Implementation for User Story 3

- [X] T045 [US3] Extend `SongOrderer` in `sb/Ordering/SongOrderer.cs` with `SpaceEfficient`:
  bounded exact permutation search (reusing `sb/PermutationsAndCombinations.cs`) up to
  `MaxPermutations`, falling back to a deterministic greedy (longest-first) heuristic beyond it
  (research.md §4) (depends on T024); make T042 pass.
  *(Partially superseded 2026-09-27 — see Phase 17: the search/fallback structure itself is
  unchanged, but `ComputeWastedSpace`/`GreedyFallback`'s pairwise-adjacent cost metric is replaced
  by one that simulates real column-fill packing, `/speckit-analyze` finding U1.)*
- [X] T046 [US3] Implement `sb documents build` in `sb/Cli/DocumentCommands.cs`: load the named
  `Document` (resolving its path via the index), flatten all chapters' songs into a
  `LeafletRequest`, call `LeafletBuilder.Build`, and write `Leaflet.Document` to
  `<document's indexed path>/main.tex`, per `contracts/cli-commands.md`'s full error list
  (unknown document, zero songs/FR-012, non-positive `--max-permutations`,
  index/filesystem mismatch/FR-023) (depends on T025, T035, T036, T037, T038, T039, T045); make
  T043 and T044 pass.

**Checkpoint**: User Stories 1, 2, and 3 all work independently; `sb documents build` produces a
complete leaflet with a chosen physical ordering.

