## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Assign and preserve each song's singing-order number (Priority: P4)

**Goal**: Every song's singing-order number is user-assigned, unique within its document,
displayed in the built leaflet, retrievable independent of physical position, and immune to any
reordering/relayout operation.

**Independent Test**: Assign singing-order numbers to a set of songs, build the leaflet with
`--ordering as-listed`, then rebuild with `--ordering space-efficient`, and verify every song
displays the exact same singing-order number in both outputs.

### Tests for User Story 4 ⚠️

- [X] T047 [P] [US4] Extend `sb/Tests/SongStoreTests.cs` with singing-order-number uniqueness
  cases (FR-016): `Add` rejects a `SingingOrderNumber` already used by another song in the same
  document (across chapters), with a descriptive error naming the conflicting song.
- [X] T048 [P] [US4] Extend `sb/Tests/SongStoreTests.cs` with `Modify` cases: moving `--chapter`
  MUST NOT change `SingingOrderNumber` (FR-024), and changing `--singing-number` goes through
  the same uniqueness check as `Add`; also cover `GetSingingOrderNumber` (FR-017) returning the
  number independent of the song's current physical position.
- [X] T049 [P] [US4] Extend `sb/Tests/LeafletBuilderTests.cs` with a **regression** case (the
  display behavior itself was already implemented and tested in T014/T025) confirming that,
  across both `AsListed` and `SpaceEfficient` builds of the same songs (now that T045/T046 make
  `SpaceEfficient` available), every displayed number is still `Song.SingingOrderNumber` (never
  `PlacedSong.PhysicalPosition`) and is unchanged between the two builds (FR-008/FR-009, SC-004).
- [X] T050 [P] [US4] Extend `sb/Tests/Cli/SongCommandsTests.cs` with `sb songs modify` cases and
  the singing-number conflict error, per `contracts/cli-commands.md`.

### Implementation for User Story 4

- [X] T051 [US4] Add singing-order-number uniqueness enforcement to `SongStore.Add` in
  `sb/Songs/SongStore.cs`: before insert, query all songs whose `chapter_id` joins to the same
  `document_id` (per `contracts/storage-format.md`) and reject on conflict (depends on T037);
  make T047 pass. *(Uniqueness check itself is unaffected by the 2026-09-26 storage-format
  change — see Phase 8 T063, which preserves this check against the index mirror.)*
- [X] T052 [US4] Implement `SongStore.Modify` (title/writer/melody/chapter/singing-number) and
  `SongStore.GetSingingOrderNumber` in `sb/Songs/SongStore.cs`, preserving `SingingOrderNumber`
  across a chapter move and re-running the uniqueness check on a number change (depends on T051);
  make T048 pass. *(Rewritten alongside T063 to read/write `number` from the single `.yml` file
  rather than the index alone.)*
- [X] T053 [US4] Regression check only — no rendering change expected: confirm
  `LeafletBuilder` (`sb/Leaflets/LeafletBuilder.cs`, implemented in T025) still displays
  `Song.SingingOrderNumber` next to each song once `SongOrderer.SpaceEfficient` (T045) is in the
  mix; fix only if T049 reveals a regression (depends on T025, T045); make T049 pass.
- [X] T054 [US4] Implement `sb songs modify` in `sb/Cli/SongCommands.cs` and wire the
  singing-number conflict error (depends on T052, T041); make T050 pass.

**Checkpoint**: All four user stories are independently functional; the full `sb documents build`
flow (format + structure + ordering + numbering) works end-to-end.

