  `song.Text` on `\n` directly (trimming each line, skipping blank ones — unchanged from the old
  whole-line fallback), escape each non-empty line, and wrap it with the existing `LineWrapper`
  only if it's too wide for `maxWidth` — no tokenizing on sentence punctuation or commas.
- [x] T089 [P] Update `sb/Tests/LeafletBuilderTests.cs`: rename
  `Build_MultiColumn_BreaksAnOverlongPhraseAcrossLinesInsteadOfOverflowing` to reflect "line" not
  "phrase" terminology (behavior unchanged — it already used a single punctuation-free line); add
  `Build_PreservesTheUsersOwnLineBreaks_WithoutMergingOrSplittingAtPunctuation` asserting that a
  song with `"first line, with a comma.\nsecond line! more text."` renders both lines verbatim,
  each ending in its own `\\`, rather than being re-split at the comma/sentence punctuation.
- [x] T090 [US1] Rewrite `sb/Tests/AggregateAccuracyTests.cs`'s SC-002 test: measure how often a
  real fixture's own non-empty input lines already fit one output line at the narrower
  multi-column width (`LineWrapper.Wrap(line, ...).Count == 1`), instead of measuring
  `PhraseSplitter` output; update the SC-003 test to build its `Column`s from plain non-empty
  input lines instead of `PhraseSplitter.Split(...)`.
- [x] T091 [P] Update `sb/specification.md` §2.1 (Formatting) to describe trusting the user's own
  line breaks, with wrapping only for over-wide lines — removing the phrase-detection language.
