  becomes an `Argument<T>` added to the command's `Arguments` (in the order matching the
  corresponding `Cli/*Commands.cs` method's parameter order); every remaining `Option<T>` gains a
  second constructor argument (its single-letter alias), scoped independently per command (e.g.
  `-m` means `--melody` in `songs add`/`modify` but `--max-permutations` in `documents build` —
