## Phase 17: 2026-09-27 Delta 10 — sequential column-fill, long-song pagination (FR-025/FR-026); A4 confirmed

**Purpose**: Apply the tenth `/speckit-clarify` round's changes, driven by the project's own
working notes on multi-column layout for long songs (`notes`, repo root), **as corrected by
`/speckit-analyze` finding U1's remediation** (a follow-up user clarification revealed the general
multi-column model was never one-song-per-column-per-row): (1) `as-listed` ordering never
reorders songs, only page/column break placement may adjust (FR-006 revision, research.md §16 —
`SongOrderer`'s *output order* itself needs no change); (2) multi-column layout fills each column
*sequentially* with as many whole songs as fit — not one song per column per row — per
`PageMetrics.LinesPerPage` (research.md §5, supersedes T019); (3) within that general algorithm, a
song too long to fit in its current column is chunked across as many further columns/pages as
needed, with a *starting*-page placement rule based on physical-page parity (FR-025,
research.md §15) — it never reserves a whole page exclusively for one song; (4) page/column
capacity (`LinesPerPage`) is derived from `sb/template-main.tex`'s own `geometry` margins and
`\fontsize` at build time, never hardcoded (FR-026, research.md §14); (5) the paper size feeding
that calculation is a fixed A4 constant (≈845.05pt height), since the user confirmed
`template-main.tex`'s `geometry` package will always specify `a4paper` (already added to the
template); (6) `SongOrderer.SpaceEfficient`'s cost function (T045) is corrected to score
candidate orderings by simulating this same real column-fill packing, replacing its stale
pairwise-adjacent approximation. See data-model.md's new `SongBlock`/`PageLayout` entities and
revised `Column`, and both `contracts/leaflet-builder-api.md`/`latex-output-contract.md`'s
updated pre/postconditions.

- [X] T110 [P] Add `PageMetrics` (`sb/Leaflets/PageMetrics.cs`): an immutable holder for
  `PaperHeightPt`, `TopMarginPt`, `BottomMarginPt`, `BaselineSkipPt`, `UsableHeightPt`,
  `LinesPerPage` (data-model.md's `PageMetrics` field table, FR-026).
- [X] T111 [US1] Add `PageMetricsReader` (`sb/Leaflets/PageMetricsReader.cs`, depends on T110):
  given a template's raw text, parse the `geometry` package's `tmargin` option (falling back to
