**Implementation addendum (title/lyrics separation)**: while implementing T114/T116, comparing
`git status` surfaced a new reference file, `sb/Kottar i karburatorn.tex` (the exact example
named in the project's working notes, "Use example from Kottar i karburatorn.tex"). Re-reading it
alongside `sb/Tests/TestFiles/TeX/test.tex` revealed both render a song's title/melody as its own
block, separate from its lyrics — not the combined per-song block every implementation since
Phase 3 had rendered (including this phase's own T114/T116 as first written). Confirmed with the
user and implemented as part of this phase (not a new phase): `SongBlock` gained `TitleLineCount`,
`Column` gained `LeadingTitleLineCount`, and `ColumnBalancer.Render` now splits each page's
columns into a title-row (paired if both columns start fresh songs there, else rendered alone at
that column's own width) followed by a body-row. See research.md §5's addendum and
data-model.md's updated `SongBlock`/`Column` for the full rationale. `dotnet test` re-confirmed
green after this addendum (126/126) — see T122's re-run.

**Implementation addendum 2 (two rendering bugs found via manual real-world testing)**: manual
testing with real Swedish-language fixtures (a long song correctly overflowing into a second
column, a following song correctly continuing onto the next page) surfaced two defects in the
title/lyrics-separation work above — both confirmed via a minimal LaTeX reproduction compiled with
the real template (`xelatex`), not just unit tests: (1) a lone title on the *right* column
rendered with no `\hspace` offset, appearing flush against the left margin instead of under the
right column (the reported "stray line"); (2) `\paragraph*{...}` (via `titlesec`) silently
produces no visible output at all when nothing follows it in the same paragraph — exactly the case
for any title with no melody line, once extracted into its own box. Fixed:
`ColumnBalancer.RenderLoneMinipage` now takes an optional preceding-offset width for a lone right
box, and every extracted title gets a trailing `\mbox{}`. Added three focused
`ColumnBalancerTests` cases constructing `PageLayout`/`Column` directly (decoupled from `Fill`,
whose packing logic was unaffected) to cover both fixes. See research.md §5's second addendum.
`dotnet test`: 129/129 passing.

**Superseded 2026-09-28**: both addenda above describe the title/lyrics-separation feature
(`SongBlock.TitleLineCount`/`Column.LeadingTitleLineCount`, and the title-row-then-body-row
rendering it enabled) as shipped, current behavior. It was later **reverted** by direct
instruction — confirmed against `sb/Leaflets/ColumnBalancer.cs`'s own doc comment and the absence
of both fields from the shipped `SongBlock`/`Column` types: a song's title/melody and lyrics
render together as one unbroken block again, with no separate leading-title row or cross-column
title pairing. This revert has no corresponding task/phase of its own — it was never recorded at
the time it happened. See research.md §5's superseded note and `contracts/latex-output-contract.md`'s
revised "Title/lyrics rendering" bullet for the current, accurate description.

