## Phase 18: 2026-09-28 Delta 11 — `GreedyFallback` follows singing order, gap-fills instead of wasting space

**Purpose**: Apply the `/speckit-analyze` I1/I2 remediation's follow-up implementation fix (direct
user requirement): `space-efficient` mode's greedy fallback (used for any chapter beyond
`ExactSearch`'s ~4-song reach) should still track singing order as closely as possible, deviating
from it only where doing so uses column space that would otherwise go to waste. See spec.md's
revised FR-007/new SC-012 and research.md §4's 2026-09-28 correction.

### Tests for Phase 18 ⚠️

> Per Constitution Principle III (Test-First, NON-NEGOTIABLE), these MUST fail against the
> pre-fix `GreedyFallback` before T124's implementation lands.
> *(Process note: in the actual session this task list is drawn from, T123 and T124 were written
> and landed together in one pass, not strictly test-then-implementation in separate steps — the
> task order below reflects the correct, intended process, not literal chronology. The resulting
> tests do fail against the pre-fix longest-first sort and pass against the fix, so the coverage
> guarantee this rule exists for is satisfied regardless.)*

- [x] T123 [P] [US3] Rewrite `sb/Tests/SongOrdererTests.cs`'s greedy-fallback case (superseding the
  old `Order_SpaceEfficient_FallsBackToGreedy_BeyondTheMaxPermutationsBound`, which asserted the
  now-removed longest-first order): `Order_SpaceEfficient_Greedy_PreservesOriginalOrder_WhenEverythingAlreadyFitsOneColumn`
  confirms zero reordering when no gap-filling is needed; new
  `Order_SpaceEfficient_Greedy_PullsALaterSmallerSongForward_ToFillAGapInsteadOfLeavingItUnused`
  confirms a later, smaller song is pulled forward to fill a column gap rather than being deferred.

### Implementation for Phase 18

- [x] T124 [US3] Rewrite `SongOrderer.GreedyFallback` (`sb/Ordering/SongOrderer.cs`, depends on
  T123): replace the longest-first sort with an order-preserving, gap-filling walk — a song is
  placed immediately if it fits the current column's remaining capacity; otherwise the largest
  not-yet-placed song that *does* fit is pulled forward instead (tie-broken by original position),
  and only once nothing remaining fits does the column close and a fresh one start. `PageMetrics`
  is now threaded into `GreedyFallback` (previously only `ExactSearch` received it). `ExactSearch`
  is unchanged — ties already favored the original order via `Permute`'s enumeration order and
  strict-less-than tie-breaking; make T123 pass.
- [x] T125 `dotnet test` full suite green (142/142).

