## Dependencies & Execution Order

### Phase Dependencies

- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — start immediately.
- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup — BLOCKS all user stories.
- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Foundational only. No dependency on US2/US3/US4.
- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on Foundational only (uses `Song` from T003, not on US1's
  engine). Independently testable without US1.
- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: Depends on US1 (`LeafletBuilder`, T025) and US2 (`DocumentStore`/
  `ChapterStore`/`SongStore`, T035–T038) to implement `sb documents build`; extends US1's
  `SongOrderer` (T024).
- **User Story 4 (Phase 6)**: Depends on US2's `SongStore` (T037) and US1's `LeafletBuilder`
  (T025); independent of US3's ordering logic itself (only shares the `build` command surface).
- **Polish (Phase 7)**: Depends on all four user stories being complete.
- **2026-09-26 Delta (Phase 8)**: Depends on Phase 7 (all prior tasks) being complete — it
  modifies `SongStore`/`Song`/`LocationMismatchDetector` in place and removes Config, so it must
  land after, not alongside, the tasks it supersedes.
- **2026-09-26 Delta 2 (Phase 9)**: Independent of Phase 8 (different files: `Document`/
  `DocumentStore`/`DocumentTemplate`/`LeafletRequest`/`CliRoot` vs. `Song`/`SongStore`/
  `LocationMismatchDetector`/Config) but sequenced after it here since both landed the same day.
- **2026-09-26 Delta 3 (Phase 10)**: Depends on Phase 9 (touches the same `DocumentStore`/
  `DocumentCommands.Build` it just rewrote).
- **2026-09-26 Delta 4 (Phase 11)**: Independent of Phases 8–10 (different files — `SongCommands`
  only), sequenced last here since it landed last.
- **2026-09-26 Delta 5 (Phase 12)**: Independent of Phases 8–11 (different files — `Formatting/`,
  `LeafletBuilder`), sequenced last since it landed last.
- **2026-09-26 Delta 6 (Phase 13)**: Depends on Phase 12 (touches the same `LeafletBuilder.cs`
  Phase 12 just rewrote).
- **2026-09-26 Delta 7 (Phase 14)**: Independent of Phases 8–13 (touches only `CliRoot.cs`),
  sequenced last since it landed last.
- **2026-09-26 Delta 8 (Phase 15)**: Depends on Phase 13 (touches the same `LeafletBuilder.cs`
  Phase 13 rewrote); independent of Phase 14.
- **2026-09-26 Delta 9 (Phase 16)**: Depends on Phase 14 (touches the same `CliRoot.cs` build
  command Phase 14 just rewrote).
- **2026-09-27 Delta 10 (Phase 17)**: Depends on Phase 13 (touches the same `LeafletBuilder.cs`
  Phase 13 rewrote to render chapters independently), Phase 15 (the same file's blank-line
  handling in `RenderSongBlock` must survive this rework), Phase 3 (supersedes `ColumnBalancer`'s
  original `RenderRow`, T019), and Phase 5 (reworks `SongOrderer`'s `SpaceEfficient` cost function,
  T045, while keeping its bounded-search/greedy-fallback structure); independent of Phases 14/16
  (`CliRoot` wiring, untouched here).
- **2026-09-28 Delta 11 (Phase 18)**: Depends on Phase 5 (rewrites the `GreedyFallback` T045
  introduced) and Phase 17 (touches the same `SongOrderer.cs` `SpaceEfficient` cost-function rework,
  T115, though a different method within it — `ComputeWastedSpace`/`ExactSearch` are untouched);
  independent of all CLI-wiring phases (14/16) and of Phases 8–13/15–16 (different file).

### Within Each User Story

- Tests are written first and MUST fail before implementation (Constitution Principle III).
- Entities/value types before the components that consume them.
- Store/engine logic before the CLI command that wires it up.

### Parallel Opportunities

- All Setup tasks marked [P] can run together; all Foundational tasks marked [P] (T003–T009) can
  run together.
- Once Foundational is done, US1's and US2's test-writing tasks (T010–T014 and T026–T032) can
  all run in parallel with each other (different files, no shared dependency) — and, since
  neither story depends on the other, both stories' implementation tasks can proceed in parallel
  too if staffed by different people.
- US3 and US4 each depend on both US1 and US2 being complete, but do not depend on each other for
  their test-writing tasks (T042–T044 vs. T047–T050 touch different files/behaviors), though
  T046 (`build` command) should land before US4's CLI-facing tests are exercised end-to-end.

